X-ray metrology systems use X-ray-based techniques to measure material composition, crystal structure, thin-film properties, dimensions, and internal features without damaging samples. These systems are increasingly important in semiconductor fabrication, electronics manufacturing, materials research, aerospace, and automotive production.

As electronic components become smaller and more complex, conventional measurement methods may struggle to characterize buried structures and multilayer materials. X-ray diffraction (XRD), X-ray fluorescence (XRF), and X-ray reflectometry (XRR) help manufacturers inspect critical features, improve process control, and identify defects earlier.

The Asia-Pacific region leads the market, accounting for an estimated 41% of global revenue in 2025, supported by its concentration of semiconductor manufacturing and electronics production.

